{"repositoryId":1347647278,"availability":"available","full":"dyson-025/LazyQL","name":"LazyQL","description":"LazyQL — A privacy-first local AI SQL agent that lets users interact with PostgreSQL and SQLite databases using natural language, with automatic SQL generation, validation, error correction, and safe database modifications.","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":9,"forks":3,"created":"2026-08-26T18:08:27Z","updated":"2026-09-01T17:40:25Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://lazy-ql.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://lazy-ql.vercel.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-20T05:27:51.569Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-20T05:27:51.569Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-20T05:27:51.569Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-20T05:27:51.569Z","stars":9,"forks":3}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["LazyQL is an AI-powered database assistant that converts natural-language questions into SQL queries using the actual schema of a connected database.","It supports SQLite and PostgreSQL, allowing users to connect a database, automatically inspect its schema, ask questions in natural language, generate SQL using Gemini, review the query, and execute it to retrieve results.","SQL is powerful, but users need to understand database schemas, table relationships, column names, and SQL syntax before they can query a database effectively."],"features":["Figure out the correct tables and columns.","Write the SQL query.","Execute and inspect the results."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/dyson-025/LazyQL/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"4b323e1cbc59fa009e4599d1de7670cfca64faaf70e518f1debbd77b1d7d6b1b","extractedAt":"2026-10-20T05:27:51.788Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-20T05:27:51.788Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"LazyQL is an AI-powered database assistant that converts natural-language questions into SQL queries using the actual schema of a connected database.","